# Evaluating a literal always yields an object of (preference)

Standing user preference: Evaluating a literal always yields an object of the corresponding declared type (e.g., Echo, Drop, Mist).

## Conventions
- Evaluating a literal always yields an object of the corresponding declared type (e.g., Echo, Drop, Mist).

